Since $\angle ABC = \alpha$, we have $\angle ABD = \alpha$. 
Since $\angle ABC = \angle DBE + \angle EBC$, we have $\alpha = \alpha + \angle EBC$. Thus, $\angle EBC = 0$, which is impossible. 

Let $BD = DE = EC = t$. Then $BC = 3t$. Let $\angle BAD = x$, $\angle DAE = y$, and $\angle EAC = z$. 
Also, let $\angle ABD = \alpha$, $\angle DBE = \beta$, $\angle EBC = \gamma$, $\angle BEC = \delta$, $\angle ECD = \epsilon$, and $\angle DEC = \zeta$. 
