We are given the following system of equations:
$$x + y = 7$$
$$x - y = 9$$
We can add the two equations to eliminate $y$:
$$(x+y) + (x-y) = 7 + 9$$
$$2x = 16$$
$$x = \frac{16}{2}$$
$$x = 8$$
Now we can substitute the value of $x$ into the first equation to find $y$:
$$8 + y = 7$$
$$y = 7 - 8$$
$$y = -1$$
So, $x = 8$ and $y = -1$.

We can check the solution by plugging the values of $x$ and $y$ into both equations:
$$x + y = 8 + (-1) = 7$$
$$x - y = 8 - (-1) = 8 + 1 = 9$$
The solution is correct.

